cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use gpbiometricspy, please cite the software version used in your analysis and the original methodological sources for specialized analyses."
title: "gpbiometricspy: Python tools for Gazepoint biometric workflows"
type: software
abstract: >-
  gpbiometricspy is a Python port of gpbiometrics 2.0.0 providing Gazepoint-native
  workflows for EDA/GSR/SCR, PPG/HRV, pupil, gaze, fixation, AOI, TTL/event
  alignment, multimodal quality control, analysis, plotting, reporting, simulation,
  reproducibility, and interoperability.
authors:
  - family-names: Balaskas
    given-names: Stefanos
    affiliation: "University of Patras"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2444-9796"
keywords:
  - Gazepoint
  - eye tracking
  - biometrics
  - electrodermal activity
  - heart rate variability
  - photoplethysmography
  - pupillometry
  - multimodal research
  - scientific Python
version: 0.1.1
date-released: 2026-08-28
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/stefanosbalaskas/gpbiometricspy"
url: "https://stefanosbalaskas.github.io/gpbiometricspy/"
